1
00:00:01,839 --> 00:00:05,594
Chapter 80. the nut.

2
00:00:05,595 --> 00:00:11,039
If the sperm whale be physioogically a sphinx, to the phenologist, his brain

3
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:16,318
seems that geometrical circle which it is impossible to square.

4
00:00:16,319 --> 00:00:21,435
In the full grown creature, the skull will measure at least 20 ft in length.

5
00:00:21,436 --> 00:00:26,558
Unhinge the lower jaw, and the side view of this skull is as the side of a

6
00:00:26,559 --> 00:00:31,594
moderately inclined plane resting throughout on a level base. But in life,

7
00:00:31,595 --> 00:00:37,198
as we have elsewhere seen, this inclined plane is angularly filled up and almost

8
00:00:37,199 --> 00:00:42,954
squared by the enormous super incumbent mass of the junk and sperm. At the high

9
00:00:42,955 --> 00:00:47,838
end of the skull forms a crater to bed that part of the mass, while under the

10
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:53,039
long floor of this crater, in another cavity seldom exceeding 10 in in length

11
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:59,198
and as many in depth, reposes the mere handful of this monster's brain. The

12
00:00:59,199 --> 00:01:03,914
brain is at least 20 ft from his apparent forehead in life. It is hidden

13
00:01:03,915 --> 00:01:09,198
away behind its vast outworks, like the innermost citadel within the amplified

14
00:01:09,199 --> 00:01:15,039
fortifications of Quebec. So like a choice casket is it secreted in him,

15
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:19,198
that I have known some whalemen who pereremptly deny that the sperm whale

16
00:01:19,199 --> 00:01:24,318
has any other brain than that palpable semblance of one formed by the cubic

17
00:01:24,319 --> 00:01:30,159
yards of his sperm magazine, lying in strange folds, courses, and convolutions

18
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:34,878
to their apprehensions. It seems more in keeping with the idea of his general

19
00:01:34,879 --> 00:01:40,399
might to regard that mystic part of him as the seat of his intelligence.

20
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:45,999
It is plain then that phenologically the head of this Leviathan in the creature's

21
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,914
living intact state is an entire delusion. As for his true brain, you can

22
00:01:51,915 --> 00:01:54,799
see no indications of it nor feel any.

23
00:01:54,800 --> 00:02:02,079
The whale, like all things that are mighty, wears a false brow to the common world.

24
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:07,115
If you unload his skull of its heaps and then take a rear view of its

25
00:02:07,116 --> 00:02:12,558
rear end, which is the high end, you will be struck by its resemblance to the

26
00:02:12,559 --> 00:02:17,039
human skull, beheld in the same situation and from the same point of

27
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:23,115
view. Indeed, place this reversed skull scaled down to the human magnitude among

28
00:02:23,116 --> 00:02:28,238
a plate of men's skulls, and you would involuntarily confound it with them, and

29
00:02:28,239 --> 00:02:33,198
remarking the depressions on one part of its summit in phenological phrase, you

30
00:02:33,199 --> 00:02:38,799
would say, "This man had no self-esteem and no veneration." And by those

31
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:43,198
negations considered along with the affirmative fact of his prodigious bulk

32
00:02:43,199 --> 00:02:47,518
and power, you can best form to yourself the truest, though not the most

33
00:02:47,519 --> 00:02:53,198
exhilarating conception of what the most exalted potency is.

34
00:02:53,199 --> 00:02:57,914
But if from the comparative dimensions of the whale's proper brain, you deem it

35
00:02:57,915 --> 00:03:03,435
incapable of being adequately charted, then I have another idea for you. If you

36
00:03:03,436 --> 00:03:08,318
attentively regard almost any quadriped spine, you will be struck by the

37
00:03:08,319 --> 00:03:13,755
resemblance of its vertebrae to a strung necklace of dwarfed skulls, all bearing

38
00:03:13,756 --> 00:03:18,799
rudimental resemblance to the skull proper. It is a German conceit that the

39
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:24,238
vertebrae are absolutely undeveloped skulls. But the curious external

40
00:03:24,239 --> 00:03:29,359
resemblance, I take it the Germans were not the first men to perceive. A foreign

41
00:03:29,360 --> 00:03:34,238
friend once pointed it out to me in the skeleton of a foe he had slain, and with

42
00:03:34,239 --> 00:03:39,198
the vertebrae of which he was inlaying in a sort of baso relievo, the beaked

43
00:03:39,199 --> 00:03:44,479
prow of his canoe. Now I consider that the phronologists have omitted an

44
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:48,479
important thing in not pushing their investigations from the cerebellum

45
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:53,359
through the spinal canal, for I believe that much of a man's character will be

46
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:58,399
found be tokened in his backbone. I would rather feel your spine than your

47
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:04,159
skull, whoever you are. A thin joist of a spine never yet upheld a full and

48
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:10,479
noble soul. I rejoice in my spine, as in the firm, audacious staff of that flag

49
00:04:10,480 --> 00:04:14,079
which I fling half out to the world.

50
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:19,435
Apply this spinal branch of phronology to the sperm whale. His cranial cavity

51
00:04:19,436 --> 00:04:23,914
is continuous with the first neck vertebrae. And in that vertebrae, the

52
00:04:23,915 --> 00:04:29,999
bottom of the spinal canal will measure 10 in across, being 8 in height, and of

53
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:34,479
a triangular figure with the base downwards. As it passes through the

54
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:39,594
remaining vertebrae, the canal tapers in size, but for a considerable distance

55
00:04:39,595 --> 00:04:44,719
remains of large capacity. Now, of course, this canal is filled with much

56
00:04:44,720 --> 00:04:50,558
the same strangely fibrous substance, the spinal cord, as the brain and

57
00:04:50,559 --> 00:04:52,954
directly communicates with the brain.

58
00:04:52,955 --> 00:04:57,838
And what is still more, for many feet after emerging from the brain's cavity,

59
00:04:57,839 --> 00:05:02,479
the spinal cord remains of an undecreasing girth almost equal to that

60
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:07,115
of the brain. Under all these circumstances, would it be unreasonable

61
00:05:07,116 --> 00:05:12,318
to survey and map out the whale's spine phenologically? For viewed in this

62
00:05:12,319 --> 00:05:16,954
light, the wonderful comparative smallness of his brain proper is more

63
00:05:16,955 --> 00:05:23,115
than compensated by the wonderful comparative magnitude of his spinal cord.

64
00:05:23,116 --> 00:05:27,435
But leaving this hint to operate as it may with the phronologist, I would

65
00:05:27,436 --> 00:05:31,755
merely assume the spinal theory for a moment in reference to the sperm whale's

66
00:05:31,756 --> 00:05:37,039
hump. This august hump, if I mistake not, rises over one of the larger

67
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:42,558
vertebrae, and is therefore in some sort the outer convex mold of it. From its

68
00:05:42,559 --> 00:05:47,838
relative situation, then I should call this high hump the organ of firmness or

69
00:05:47,839 --> 00:05:53,115
indomitableness in the sperm whale, and that the great monster is indomitable,

70
00:05:53,116 --> 00:05:57,800
you will yet have reason to know.
